{'symbol': 'AAPL', 'date': '2020-02-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'Apple Says Does Not Expect To Meet Revenue Guidance Provided For March Quarter', 'text': 'Feb 17  - Apple Inc <AAPL.O>::INVESTOR UPDATE ON QUARTERLY GUIDANCE.APPLE INC - DO NOT EXPECT TO MEET REVENUE GUIDANCE PROVIDED FOR MARCH QUARTER DUE TO TWO MAIN FACTORS.APPLE INC - WORK IS STARTING TO RESUME AROUND CHINA , BUT WE ARE EXPERIENCING A SLOWER RETURN TO NORMAL CONDITIONS THAN WE HAD ANTICIPATED.APPLE INC - IPHONE MANUFACTURING PARTNER SITES LOCATED OUTSIDE HUBEI ARE RAMPING UP MORE SLOWLY THAN HAD ANTICIPATED.APPLE INC - WORLDWIDE IPHONE SUPPLY WILL BE TEMPORARILY CONSTRAINED.APPLE INC - IPHONE SUPPLY SHORTAGES WILL TEMPORARILY AFFECT REVENUES WORLDWIDE.APPLE INC - DEMAND FOR PRODUCTS WITHIN CHINA HAS BEEN AFFECTED.APPLE INC - CORPORATE OFFICES AND CONTACT CENTERS IN CHINA ARE OPEN, AND OUR ONLINE STORES HAVE REMAINED OPEN THROUGHOUT.APPLE INC - OUTSIDE OF CHINA, CUSTOMER DEMAND ACROSS PRODUCT AND SERVICE CATEGORIES HAS BEEN STRONG TO DATE AND IN LINE WITH EXPECTATIONS.'}
